RESOLUTION OF THE FOUNDING MEMBERS COUNCIL AND BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF [COMPANY NAME] LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY (Constitutional Resolution adopted on [FULL DATE])

WHEREAS the Company is to be incorporated as a foreign-invested limited liability company under the laws of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam;

WHEREAS the founding members have unanimously agreed on the charter capital, registered office, and management structure;

NOW, THEREFORE, IT IS RESOLVED AS FOLLOWS:

1. SHARE CAPITAL SUBSCRIPTION. The total charter capital of the Company is approved and ratified as the sum set forth in the Company Charter, and all founding members hereby subscribe to their respective capital contributions in accordance with the subscribed schedules. The members unanimously direct management to make such capital available and paid in full within ninety (90) days following issuance of the Enterprise Registration Certificate.

2. REGISTERED OFFICE ADOPTION. The registered office of the Company shall be established at [ADDRESS, WARD, DISTRICT, PROVINCE/CITY, VIETNAM] and the necessary lease agreement or lawful use document for such premises is hereby approved. The General Director is authorized to execute and file all documents evidencing the registered office with the Department of Planning and Investment.

3. OFFICER APPOINTMENTS. The following persons are appointed to the management positions indicated, effective as of the adoption of this Resolution:
   (a) [NAME] as Chairman of the Members Council;
   (b) [NAME] as General Director / Chief Executive Officer, who shall be the legal representative of the Company;
   (c) [NAME] as Chief Financial Officer;
   (d) [NAME] as Chief Accountant.
   Each officer shall discharge duties within the powers and limitations prescribed by the Company Charter and the Enterprise Law, and the General Director is expressly authorized to act as the Company representative in all incorporation proceedings.

4. AUTHORIZATION FOR INCORPORATION FILINGS. The General Director is authorized to prepare, execute, submit, and follow up on all forms, declarations, contracts, and applications required for statutory incorporation, including the Application for Enterprise Registration, the energy certificate registration, tax registration, seal sample notification, and any necessary regulatory licenses.

5. STATUTORY RECORDS. The Chairman and General Director are directed to establish and continuously maintain the statutory registers, minutes books, resolution files, and capital contribution records of the Company in accordance with Articles 49 and 183 of the Enterprise Law.

6. MISCELLANEOUS. This Resolution is adopted unanimously and enters into effect immediately. Any provisions of prior drafts or informal decisions that contradict this Resolution are hereby superseded.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, this Resolution has been executed by the founding members and appointed officers on the date first above written.
